d="pone.0067520-Cellulede1"><label>14</label><mixed-citation publication-type="book">Cellule de Planification et de Statistique du Ministere de la Sant Direction Nationale de la Statistique et de l&#x02019;Informatique du Ministere de l&#x02019;Economie del&#x02019;Industrie et du Commerce (2007) Enquete Demographique et de Sante du Mali 2006. Calverton, Maryland, USA: CPS/DNSI et Macro International Inc.</mixed-citation></ref><ref id="pone.0067520-RBM1"><label>15</label><mixed-citation publication-type="book">RBM Vector Control Working Group: Continuous Distribution Work Stream (2011) Conensus statement on continuous distribution systems for insecticide treated nets. Geneva: RBM.</mixed-citation></ref><ref id="pone.0067520-Marchant1"><label>16</label><mixed-citation publication-type="journal"><name><surname>Marchant</surname><given-names>T</given-names></name>, <name><surname>Schellenberg</surname><given-names>D</given-names></name>, <name><surname>Nathan</surname><given-names>R</given-names></name>, <name><surname>Armstrong-Schellenberg</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name>, <name><surname>Mponda</surname><given-names>H</given-names></name>, <etal>et al</etal> (<year>2010</year>) <article-title>Assessment of a national voucher scheme to deliver insecticide-treated mosquito nets to pregnant women</article-title>. <source>CMAJ</source><volume>182</volume>: <fpage>152</fpage>&#x02013;<lpage>156</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">20064944</pub-id></mixed-citation></ref><ref id="pone.0067520-Webster1"><label>17</label><mixed-citation publication-type="journal"><name><surname>Webster</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name>, <name><surname>Kweku</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name>, <name><surname>Dedzo</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name>, <name><surname>Tinkorang</surname><given-names>K</given-names></name>, <name><surname>Bruce</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name>, <etal>et al</etal> (<year>2010</year>) <article-title>Evaluating delivery systems: complex evaluations and plausibility inference</article-title>. <source>Am J Trop Med Hyg</source><volume>82</volume>: <fpage>672</fpage>&#x02013;<lpage>677</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">20348517</pub-id></mixed-citation></ref><ref id="pone.0067520-Sogoba1"><label>18</label><mixed-citation publication-type="journal"><name><surname>Sogoba</surname><given-names>N</given-names></name>, <name><surname>Doumbia</surname><given-names>S</given-names></name>, <name><surname>Vounatsou</surname><given-names>P</given-names></name>, <name><surname>Bagayoko</surname><given-names>MM</given-names></name>, <name><surname>Dolo</surname><given-names>G</given-names></name>, <etal>et al</etal> (<year>2007</year>) <article-title>Malaria transmission dynamics in Niono, Mali: the effect of the irrigation systems</article-title>. <source>Acta Trop</source><volume>101</volume>: <fpage>232</fpage>&#x02013;<lpage>240</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">17362859</pub-id></mixed-citation></ref><ref id="pone.0067520-MEASURE1"><label>19</label><mixed-citation publication-type="book">MEASURE Evaluation (2001) Sampling Manual for Facility Surveys for Population, Maternal Health, child Health and STD Programs in Developing Countries. Chapel Hill: Carolina Population Center, Universtiy of North Carolina at Chapel Hill.</mixed-citation></ref><ref id="pone.0067520-World6"><label>20</label><mixed-citation publication-type="book">World Health Organisation (2007) Malaria in Pregnancy: Guidelines for measuring key monitoring and evaluation indicators. Geneva: WHO.</mixed-citation></ref><ref id="pone.0067520-Programme1"><label>21</label><mixed-citation publication-type="book">Programme National de Lutte Contre le Paludisme (2003) Politique Nationale de Lutte Contre le Paludisme. Bamako: PNLP.</mixed-citation></ref><ref id="pone.0067520-Lauritsen1"><label>22</label><mixed-citation publication-type="book">Lauritsen J (2000&#x02013;2008) EpiData Data Entry, Data Management and Basic Statistical Analysis System Version 3.1. Odense, Denmark: EpiData Association.</mixed-citation></ref><ref id="pone.0067520-StataCorp1"><label>23</label><mixed-citation publication-type="book">Stata Corp LP (2007) Stata Data Analysis &#x00026; Statistical Sortware Version 11. College Station, Texas.</mixed-citation></ref><ref id="pone.0067520-ODonnell1"><label>24</label><mixed-citation publication-type="book">O&#x02019;Donnell O, van Doorslaer E, Wagstaff A, Lindelow M (2008) Analyzing Health Equity Using Household Survey Data. Washington, D.C.: The World Bank.</mixed-citation></ref><ref id="pone.0067520-McKenzie1"><label>25</label><mixed-citation publication-type="book">McKenzie DJ (2005) Measuring inequality with asset indicators. Journal of Population Economics 18.</mixed-citation></ref><ref id="pone.0067520-Vyas1"><label>26</label><mixed-citation publication-type="journal"><name><surname>Vyas</surname><given-names>S</given-names></name>, <name><surname>Kumaranayake</surname><given-names>L</given-names></name> (<year>2006</year>) <article-title>Constructing socio-economic status indices: how to use principal components analysis</article-title>. <source>Health Policy Plan</source><volume>21</volume>: <fpage>459</fpage>&#x02013;<lpage>468</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">17030551</pub-id></mixed-citation></ref><ref id="pone.0067520-Filmer1"><label>27</label><mixed-citation publication-type="book">Filmer D, Pritchett L (1998) Estimating wealth effects without expenditure data - or tears: Educational enrolment in India. Development Economics Research Group. Washington DC: The World Bank.</mixed-citation></ref><ref id="pone.0067520-Carlson1"><label>28</label><mixed-citation publication-type="journal"><name><surname>Carlson</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name>, <name><surname>Smith Paintain</surname><given-names>L</given-names></name>, <name><surname>Bruce</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name>, <name><surname>Webster</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name>, <na